    "dc.description.abstract" : [ {
      "value" : "The main goal of hyperspectral band selection is to select a subset of bands to reduce the redundancy in hyperspectral images. Deep reinforcement learning was recently introduced for this task, which adopts a deep Q-network as the agent and information entropy for the reward scheme. In this paper, we present a similarity-based band selection approach using a double deep Q-network. We formulate and compare three reward schemes based on different similarity measurements: cosine distance, Euclidean distance and linear prediction. The experiments show that the proposed double deep Q-network framework has produced encouraging classification accuracy with different similarity-based reward schemes.",
      "language" : null,
      "authority" : null,
      "confidence" : -1,
      "place" : 0
    } ],
